In the evening, I walked back to the station.
I got onto the S-Bahn.
Almost nobody spoke in the carriage anymore.
The other day-trippers fell asleep quickly.
Many people simply fell asleep over their rucksacks.
I almost closed my eyes too.
But I stayed awake, Sofia.
I leaned my head against the window.
That way, I looked outside again.
I saw the dark pine forests.
Everything stayed very quiet outside.
Then I arrived back in Berlin.
I got out of the S-Bahn.
From there, I walked straight to the flat.
I only came home very late.
Now I am finally lying in bed.
I am really tired, but also totally happy.
This day has been beautiful.
Sleep well, Sofia!
